3. Integration: Automating the Failover (The Runbook)

With the security perimeter established, the next phase is to deploy the FinOps logic and integrate it directly into the disaster recovery sequence. The runbook must be configured to execute strictly as a Post-action, ensuring the Azure VMs are physically provisioned in the target region before the script attempts to modify their disks.

3.1. Importing and Publishing the Runbook

In the Azure Portal, navigate to the Automation Account you created in the previous step.

In the left-hand menu, under Process Automation, click on Runbooks.

Click + Create a runbook at the top.

Name: ASR-SmartTiering-PremiumUpgrade

Runbook type: PowerShell

Runtime version: 5.1 (or 7.1/7.2 depending on your standard)

[Screen: The "Create a runbook" pane showing the Name and Runbook type (PowerShell) fields filled out]

Click Create. You will be redirected to the PowerShell editor.

Paste the validated FinOps Smart Tiering PowerShell script into the editor pane.

Click Save at the top left, and then—critically—click Publish.

Note: ASR Recovery Plans cannot see or execute runbooks that are left in "Edit" or "Draft" mode.

[Screen: The Runbook editor showing the script pasted inside, with a red box highlighting the "Publish" button at the top]

3.2. Integrating the Runbook into the ASR Recovery Plan

Navigate to your Recovery Services Vault (where the ASR replication is managed).

In the left menu, under Manage, click on Recovery Plans (Site Recovery).

[Screen: The left menu of the Recovery Services Vault with a red box around "Recovery Plans (Site Recovery)"]

Click on the target Recovery Plan for the application (e.g., RP-ANTARES).

At the top of the Recovery Plan overview, click Customize.

[Screen: The Recovery Plan overview page with the "Customize" button highlighted at the top]

Locate the VM startup group, typically Group 1: Start.

Click the ... (ellipsis) on the right side of the Group 1: Start row and select Add post action.

Warning: Never add this as a Pre-action. The script relies on the "Time Created" attribute of the newly spawned disks, which do not exist until the Post-action phase.

[Screen: The customization view showing the expanded Group 1, highlighting the "... > Add post action" dropdown menu]

In the Insert action blade that opens on the right, fill in the following:

Action to perform: Script

Name: FinOps-UpgradeDisks-Premium

Automation account: Select the automation account created in Section 2.

Runbook name: Select ASR-SmartTiering-PremiumUpgrade.

[Screen: The "Insert action" blade fully populated with the Automation account and Runbook details]

Click OK to close the blade.

Click Save at the top of the Customize page to commit the new architecture.
